{"claims":[{"excerpt":"Explain how CPython 3.13’s experimental free-threading configuration connects an application’s runtime choice to what happens when it imports an extension.","claim":"The runtime choice to use CPython 3.13’s experimental free-threading configuration is relevant to what happens when an application imports an extension.","category":"technical","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"CPython 3.13 introduced experimental free threading, a configuration that can run with the global interpreter lock disabled. An extension must explicitly indicate that it supports this mode; importing one without that declaration warns and enables the GIL.","narrative":"Explain how CPython 3.13’s experimental free-threading configuration connects an application’s runtime choice to what happens when it imports an extension.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"This accurately frames the source’s connection between the free-threading configuration and extension-import behavior.","materiality":"Central framing; no material discrepancy."},{"excerpt":"In this mode, importing an extension without an explicit support declaration produces a warning and enables the GIL.","claim":"In CPython 3.13 free-threading mode, importing an extension without an explicit support declaration produces a warning and enables the GIL.","category":"outcome","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"An extension must explicitly indicate that it supports this mode; importing one without that declaration warns and enables the GIL.","narrative":"In this mode, importing an extension without an explicit support declaration produces a warning and enables the GIL.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The narrative preserves the source’s condition and both stated import outcomes.","materiality":"Material behavior, accurately stated."},{"excerpt":"The declaration mechanism differs between multi-phase and single-phase initialization.","claim":"The way an ex